__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pkl
.cache/
/tmp/
.DS_Store
.env

# seleniumbase/webdriver scratch (from an abandoned FBref scrape)
downloaded_files/

# Regenerable build artifacts. Every path below is a `derived` node in src/manifest.py
# with a declared producer and declared inputs, so losing one costs CPU, not
# information — `.\fpl.ps1 doctor` names the script that rebuilds it.
#
# The inverse is the rule that matters: anything git STILL tracks under outputs/ or
# data/ is tracked precisely because NOTHING in the tree can rebuild it. Do not add a
# path here without first confirming a producer exists. predictions/ is never ignored
# — a locked board is not regenerable and is the only evidence the model can be scored.
data/E0_recon.csv
data/coldstart_hist.csv

# More of the same rule: each has a producer, so none is worth a blob.

# Hand-kept backups and dated snapshots of regenerable boards.
*.bak
data/*.gw3fetch

# Local-machine and agent scratch. .claude/agents/ IS tracked — those seven files are
# hand-written and nothing regenerates them; worktrees are abandoned copies (1.9 MB)
# and settings.local.json is per-machine.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
# hardcodes an absolute path into one machine's Python profile
.claude/launch.json

# Personal account identifier. Not a secret (it appears in the FPL site URL), but it
# identifies one manager and every user supplies their own.
data/fpl_entry_id.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# outputs/ is REGENERABLE BY DEFAULT.
#
# Stated as a default rather than a list because a list silently fails open: a new
# artifact nobody remembered to add gets committed, and the 14.5 MB blob is in history
# before anyone notices. Inverting it fails closed instead — a genuinely irreplaceable
# output is invisible to git until someone names it below, which is a deliberate act.
#
# The exceptions are the files for which NO producer exists anywhere in src/ or
# scripts/. Each was verified by grep on 2026-09-08, not assumed. If you add one here,
# first confirm nothing writes it; if you write a producer for one, delete its line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/*
!outputs/plans/
!outputs/fixtures_gw1_6.csv
!outputs/fpl_2627_team_fixtures_gw1_10_raw.csv
!outputs/fpl_gw1_6_planner.html
!outputs/fpl_projection_model.html
!outputs/projection_2627_run.csv
!outputs/team_strength_2627.csv
# Load-bearing: a 2026-08-28 roster snapshot carrying both the contemporaneous
# web_name and player_code. scripts/crosswalk_gw1_lock.py resolves the GW1 lock
# against it, so the project's only true forecast score depends on this file and
# nothing can rebuild it. Do not remove this line.
!outputs/fpl_2627_players.csv
